ages, and\n  the validation manifest, with no open interpretation questions for either a\n  gallery implementer or a tutorial author.\n- A reference tutorial package conforming to the format exists and\n  demonstrates versioning and validation independent of a Dashboard release.\n- A packaged tutorial's validation outcome is determinable from its validation\n  manifest alone (which release it was tested against, and whether it passed).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-3 (P1): \"A tutorial packaging format (metadata, pinned images,\n  validation manifest) is defined so tutorials are versioned and testable\n  independently of Dashboard releases.\" Full cover. Priority raised to P0 by\n  inheritance: this epic transitively enables the P0 gallery (HLR-1) and the\n  P0 curated tutorials (HLR-2).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":30674,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-86791b01b4177863","agent_id":"aa0c53e0a9c103d38","session_id":"bc2fac71-1701-446f-99e6-c82b84a2c07c","uuid":"8c3e9518-5f6d-4ff1-a127-7867867efcec","timestamp":"2026-10-26T12:22:08.021Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9019"}
