5 | Rule 11 (docs-authoring last) | Same. |\n68\t| E004 → E005 | Rule 11 (docs-authoring last) | Same. |\n69\t| E002 ∥ E003 ∥ E004 (no edges) | Rule 14/15 parallel + AC gate | The gallery is launch mechanics; the tutorials are content launched through it. They meet at runtime, not at build time: the coupling is expressed as an acceptance criterion on the gallery epic (end-to-end launch of a packaged tutorial succeeds), not as a DAG edge. |\n70\t| E003 ∥ E004 (no edge) | Rule 1 (different component/team) | Notebook tutorials (Notebooks/Workbenches) and the pipeline tutorial (Data Science Pipelines/RHOAI Pipelines) are independent content work in different component areas. |\n71\t\n72\tComponent mapping notes (canonical names from `.context/rhai-components.txt`):\n73\t- E001 spans Dashboard, Notebooks, and Data Science Pipelines consumption; it\n74\t  is assigned canonical component `Dashboard` because the gallery is the\n75\t  primary consumer/renderer of the format and the Dashboard team owns the\n76\t  launch contract. The span is recorded here per the component-name constraint.\n77\t- E005 is assigned canonical component `Documentation` (in the canonical list;\n78\t  no architecture-context file exists for it — see Health Warnings).\n79\t\n80\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n81\t\n82\t| HLR | Priority | Requirement (abridged) | Epics | Notes |\n83\t|-----|----------|------------------------|-------|-------|\n84\t| HLR-1 | P0 | Tutorial gallery in the Dashboard with launch into the user's project | RHAISTRAT-9019-E002 | Direct cover: gallery surface + workbench/pipeline launch mechanics. |\n85\t| HLR-2 | P0 | Six curated tutorials covering the core journeys, tested against the current release | RHAISTRAT-9019-E003, RHAISTRAT-9019-E004 | Split by component/team boundary: E003 covers the five notebook/workbench journeys (first workbench, data prep, first training run, first deployment, first RAG app); E004 covers the first-pipeline journey (Data Science Pipelines, different owning team). Together they cover all six. |\n86\t| HLR-3 | P1 | Tutorial packaging format (metadata, pinned images, validation manifest) for versioned, independently testable tutorials | RHAISTRAT-9019-E001 | Single epic — the format is one logical deliverable consumed by E002–E004. Priority raised P1→P0 by inheritance (transitively enables HLR-1 and HLR-2). |\n87\t| HLR-4 | P2 | Documentation covers using the gallery and the contribution process | RHAISTRAT-9019-E005 | Direct cover. Epic priority is P1 via the docs-authoring priority exception (strategy priority Major → P1); HLR-4 itself remains P2 in the strategy. |\n88\t\n89\tAll four HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements; no redundant/overlapping\n90\tHLR pairs (each HLR describes a distinct surface: format spec, gallery code,\n91\ttutorial content, documentation).\n92\t\n93\t## Health Warnings\n94\t\n95\t- **Missing strategy sections**: no Impacted Teams table, no Dependencies\n96\t  table, no Given/When/Then acceptance criteria, and no Non-Functional\n97\t  Requirements. Epic acceptance criteria below are derived from the HLRs; team\n98\t  assignments are inferred from architecture-context owning teams\n99\t  (Dashboard → RHOAI Dashboard, Notebooks → Workbenches, Data Science\n100\t  Pipelines → RHOAI Pipelines). Human review should confirm these.\n101\t- **Documentation team assumption**: `Documentation` has no architecture-context\n102\t  file and no owning team is stated anywhere in the strategy; E005 is assigned\n103\t  team \"RHOAI Docs\" as a placeholder for human confirmation.\n104\t- **Affected Components is a bare list** (no change/owner columns) — active vs.\n105\t  passive classification was derived from the HLRs: Dashboard is the only\n106\t  code-change component; Notebooks and Data Science Pipelines are content\n107\t  targets for tutorials; Documentation is docs-authoring.\n108\t- **Scope trap to watch**: \"Each is tested against the current release\"\n109\t  (HLR-2) presumes a repeatable validation mechanism; the decomposition counts\n110\t  on the HLR-3 packaging format's validation manifest to carry it. If tutorial\n111\t  hosting/validation infrastructure does not exist at execution time, E003/E004\n112\t  scope may grow — flagged for human review rather than pre-split.\n113\t- **Tutorial hosting location unspecified**: the strategy does not say where\n114\t  tutorial packages live (existing repos vs. a new one). Treated as an\n115\t  implementation detail for the authoring teams, not a genuine unknown (the\n116\t  answer does not change which epics exist); captured as an AC/notes item on\n117\t  E003/E004.\n118\t- No priority inversions detected.\n119\t\n120\t## Tiered Delivery\n121\t\n122\tNot applicable — no external dependencies with uncertain timing; all work is\n123\tinternal to the platform teams.\n124\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bef45a05c1660d71","agent_id":"abc4c27ef1bed2f6c","session_id":"bc2fac71-1701-446f-99e6-c82b84a2c07c","uuid":"14d11099-4b9f-4563-a70e-bc476c66a673","timestamp":"2026-10-26T12:23:47.470Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8138b7073bdc19d7","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9019 decomposition"}
