{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-93c02e76988ef7d9","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9019\n3\tepic_count: 5\n4\tcritical_path_length: 3\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\ttriage: null\n7\ttriage_rationale: null\n8\trevised: true\n9\t---\n10\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-9019 (Curated getting-started tutorial gallery)\n11\t\n12\tTriage: not below-threshold — the strategy spans multiple components (Dashboard,\n13\tNotebooks, Data Science Pipelines, Documentation), multiple teams, and multiple\n14\tarchitecturally distinct work streams (product code for the gallery and launch\n15\tmechanics, authored tutorial content, and documentation), which the problem\n16\tstatement itself calls out as \"three different kinds of work with different\n17\towners and review processes\". Not docs-only — the Dashboard requires code\n18\tchanges. Full decomposition follows.\n19\t\n20\tStrategy structure notes: the strategy provides HLRs and an Affected Components\n21\tlist, but no Impacted Teams table, no Dependencies table, no Given/When/Then\n22\tacceptance criteria, no NFRs, and no Staff Engineer Input (see Health\n23\tWarnings). Open Questions: \"None\" — no Investigation epics are warranted. Team\n24\tassignments are derived from the architecture-context owning teams.\n25\t\n26\t## Epic List\n27\t\n28\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n29\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n30\t| RHAISTRAT-9019-E001 | Define the tutorial packaging format (metadata, pinned images, validation manifest) | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P0 |\n31\t| RHAISTRAT-9019-E002 | Dashboard tutorial gallery with one-click launch into the user's project | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P0 |\n32\t| RHAISTRAT-9019-E003 | Author the notebook-based curated tutorials (first workbench, data prep, first training run, first deployment, first RAG app) | Implementation | Workbenches | P0 |\n33\t| RHAISTRAT-9019-E004 | Author the first-pipeline curated tutorial | Implementation | RHOAI Pipelines | P0 |\n34\t| RHAISTRAT-9019-E005 | Document tutorial gallery usage and the tutorial contribution process | Implementation | RHOAI Docs | P1 |\n35\t\n36\tPriority derivation:\n37\t- E002 is P0 (HLR-1 is P0).\n38\t- E003/E004 are P0 (HLR-2 is P0).\n39\t- E001 maps to HLR-3 (P1) but transitively enables the P0 gallery (HLR-1) and\n40\t  the P0 tutorials (HLR-2) — priority inheritance raises it to P0.\n41\t- E005 is a `docs-authoring` epic covering HLR-4 (P2); per the docs-authoring\n42\t  priority exception it takes its priority from the strategy frontmatter\n43\t  (`priority: Major` → P1), not from HLR-4 or from inheritance.\n44\t\n45\t## Dependency DAG\n46\t\n47\t```mermaid\n48\tgraph TD\n49\t    E001[RHAISTRAT-9019-E001 packaging format] --> E002[RHAISTRAT-9019-E002 gallery + launch]\n50\t    E001 --> E003[RHAISTRAT-9019-E003 notebook tutorials]\n51\t    E001 --> E004[RHAISTRAT-9019-E004 pipeline tutorial]\n52\t    E002 --> E005[RHAISTRAT-9019-E005 documentation]\n53\t    E003 --> E005\n54\t    E004 --> E005\n55\t    E001 --> E005\n56\t```\n57\t\n58\tCritical path: E001 → E002 (or E003/E004) → E005, length 3.\n59\t\n60\t## DAG Justification\n61\t\n62\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n63\t|------|------|-----------|\n64\t| E001 → E002 | Rule 13 (build-against artifact) | The gallery code parses tutorial metadata and launch configuration defined by the packaging format — an API/schema artifact the Dashboard implementation builds against, not a configuration reference. |\n65\t| E001 → E003 | Rule 13 (build-against artifact) | Tutorial content is packaged (metadata, pinned images, validation manifest) per the format; authoring cannot complete before the format is defined. |\n66\t| E001 → E004 | Rule 13 (build-against artifact) | Same as above for the pipeline tutorial. |\n67\t| E002 → E005 | Rule 11 (docs-authoring last) | Documentation describes what was built; blocked by every Implementation epic. |\n68\t| E003 → E005 | Rule 11 (docs-authoring last) | Same. |\n69\t| E004 → E005 | Rule 11 (docs-authoring last) | Same. |\n70\t| E001 → E005 | Rule 11 (docs-authoring last) | Same — E001 is an Implementation epic (format spec + reference package), so the docs-authoring epic is blocked by it along with all other Implementation epics. |\n71\t| E002 ∥ E003 ∥ E004 (no edges) | Rule 14/15 parallel + AC gate | The gallery is launch mechanics; the tutorials are content launched through it. They meet at runtime, not at build time: the coupling is expressed as an acceptance criterion on the gallery epic (end-to-end launch of a packaged tutorial succeeds), not as a DAG edge. |\n72\t| E003 ∥ E004 (no edge) | Rule 1 (different component/team) | Notebook tutorials (Notebooks/Workbenches) and the pipeline tutorial (Data Science Pipelines/RHOAI Pipelines) are independent content work in different component areas. |\n73\t\n74\tComponent mapping notes (canonical names from `.context/rhai-components.txt`):\n75\t- E001 spans Dashboard, Notebooks, and Data Science Pipelines consumption; it\n76\t  is assigned canonical component `Dashboard` because the gallery is the\n77\t  primary consumer/renderer of the format and the Dashboard team owns the\n78\t  launch contract. The span is recorded here per the component-name constraint.\n79\t- E005 is assigned canonical component `Documentation` (in the canonical list;\n80\t  no architecture-context file exists for it — see Health Warnings).\n81\t\n82\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n83\t\n84\t| HLR | Priority | Requirement (abridged) | Epics | Notes |\n85\t|-----|----------|------------------------|-------|-------|\n86\t| HLR-1 | P0 | Tutorial gallery in the Dashboard with launch into the user's project | RHAISTRAT-9019-E002 | Direct cover: gallery surface + workbench/pipeline launch mechanics. |\n87\t| HLR-2 | P0 | Six curated tutorials covering the core journeys, tested against the current release | RHAISTRAT-9019-E003, RHAISTRAT-9019-E004 |