{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b5880be69c4bc186","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9019-E001\n3\ttitle: Define the tutorial packaging format (metadata, pinned images, validation manifest)\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9019\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 0\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 0\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: -1\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 3\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Define the tutorial packaging format (metadata, pinned images, validation manifest)\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic defines the tutorial packaging format that makes tutorials versioned\n34\tand testable independently of Dashboard releases. The format is the shared\n35\tartifact that both the Dashboard tutorial gallery (which renders and launches\n36\ttutorials) and tutorial authors (who package content per the format) build\n37\tagainst. It covers tutorial metadata, pinned images, and a validation\n38\tmanifest, plus the versioning rules that let a tutorial be re-validated against\n39\ta platform release without a Dashboard release.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Define the tutorial metadata structure a gallery consumer reads to display\n44\t  and launch a tutorial (title, journey, tutorial type, launch configuration).\n45\t- Define the image-pinning convention so a tutorial always runs against known\n46\t  workbench/pipeline images rather than floating tags.\n47\t- Define the validation manifest: what \"tested against the current release\"\n48\t  means for a tutorial, and how validation is recorded per tutorial version.\n49\t- Define tutorial versioning rules so tutorials release and validate on their\n50\t  own cadence, decoupled from Dashboard releases.\n51\t- Produce the format specification and a reference package that demonstrates\n52\t  it end to end.\n53\t\n54\tNote: the format is consumed across the Dashboard, Notebooks, and Data Science\n55\tPipelines components; the Dashboard is the primary consumer and owns the launch\n56\tcontract, so the work is tracked under the Dashboard component.\n57\t\n58\t## Acceptance Criteria\n59\t\n60\t- A written format specification exists covering metadata, pinned images, and\n61\t  the validation manifest, with no open interpretation questions for either a\n62\t  gallery implementer or a tutorial author.\n63\t- A reference tutorial package conforming to the format exists and\n64\t  demonstrates versioning and validation independent of a Dashboard release.\n65\t- A packaged tutorial's validation outcome is determinable from its validation\n66\t  manifest alone (which release it was tested against, and whether it passed).\n67\t\n68\t## HLR Traceability\n69\t\n70\t- HLR-3 (P1): \"A tutorial packaging format (metadata, pinned images,\n71\t  validation manifest) is defined so tutorials are versioned and testable\n72\t  independently of Dashboard releases.\" Full cover. Priority raised to P0 by\n73\t  inheritance: this epic transitively enables the P0 gallery (HLR-1) and the\n74\t  P0 curated tutorials (HLR-2).\n75\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-af6523f3bbe53b4e","agent_id":"a3701fb798c825e88","session_id":"bc2fac71-1701-446f-99e6-c82b84a2c07c","uuid":"cc3c1acc-1226-43ea-ab4d-5f1ac5d07308","timestamp":"2026-10-26T12:28:09.586Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b5880be69c4bc186","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9019"}
